    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -520,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        480,
        820
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Performance Remix: stage 1, look\n\nMakes the still that stage 2 animates. Four candidates per run, about 20 seconds each.\n\n1. **Driving clip**: load the video you will animate. **Frame time** picks the frame to edit, in seconds; 0 is the first frame. Pick a frame where the performer is fully visible.\n2. **Reference 1**: the character. **Reference 2** is optional, for an outfit, a product or a place: select it and press Ctrl+B to enable it.\n3. **Prompt**: image 1 is the clip frame, image 2 is reference 1, image 3 is reference 2.\n4. Run. Candidates are saved to `output/performance-remix/`. Load the one you like into stage 2 as its reference image.\n\n**Already have the final image?** Skip this workflow and load your image straight into stage 2. Keep its framing close to the clip's (full body to full body, close-up to close-up).\n\n### Prompt recipes\n\n- **Character**: Replace the person in image 1 with the character from image 2. Keep the exact pose, body position, size in frame, camera angle and framing of image 1. Keep the character's face, hair, outfit, colors and art style from image 2. Keep the background of image 1.\n- **World**: Keep the person in image 1 exactly as they are, same pose and framing. Replace the background with <place>. Match the lighting to the new place.\n- **Style**: Redraw image 1 as <style>. Keep the pose, framing and composition exactly the same.\n- **Object**: In image 1, replace the <object> with the <object> from image 2. Keep everything else exactly the same."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Performance Remix: stage 1, look\n\nMakes the still that stage 2 animates. Four candidates per run, about 20 seconds each.\n\n1. **Driving clip**: load the video you will animate. **Frame time** picks the frame to edit, in seconds; 0 is the first frame. Pick a frame where the performer is fully visible.\n2. **Reference 1**: the character. **Reference 2** is optional, for an outfit, a product or a place: select it and press Ctrl+B to enable it.\n3. **Prompt**: image 1 is the clip frame, image 2 is reference 1, image 3 is reference 2.\n4. Run. Candidates are saved to `output/performance-remix/`. Load the one you like into stage 2 as its reference image.\n\n**Already have the final image?** Skip this workflow and load your image straight into stage 2. Keep its framing close to the clip's (full body to full body, close-up to close-up).\n\n### Prompt recipes\n\n- **Character**: Replace the person in image 1 with the character from image 2. Keep the exact pose, body position, size in frame, camera angle and framing of image 1. Keep the character's face, hair, outfit, colors and art style from image 2. Keep the background of image 1.\n- **World**: Keep the person in image 1 exactly as they are, same pose and framing. Replace the background with <place>. Match the lighting to the new place.\n- **Style**: Redraw image 1 as <style>. Keep the pose, framing and composition exactly the same.\n- **Object**: In image 1, replace the <object> with the <object> from image 2. Keep everything else exactly the same."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
